Use `FormInput` with typed fields and set the receipt ID’s regex via `TextField(pattern=...)`. Then return `ChatAssistantWorkflowOutput` with `isError=True` when the submitted expense fails validation.

```python
from datetime import date
import mistralai.workflows as workflows
import mistralai.workflows.plugins.mistralai as workflows_mistralai
from mistralai.workflows.conversational import (
    FormInput, TextField, NumberField, DateField,
)


class ExpenseForm(FormInput):
    description: str = TextField(description="Expense description")
    amount: float = NumberField(
        description="Amount in USD",
        minimum=0,
        maximum=10_000,
    )
    expense_date: date = DateField(description="Date of expense")
    receipt_id: str = TextField(
        description="Receipt ID",
        pattern=r"^RCP-\d{6}$",
    )


@workflows.workflow.define(
    name="expense-validation-workflow",
    workflow_display_name="Expense Validation",
    workflow_description="Collects and validates an expense",
)
class ExpenseValidationWorkflow(workflows.InteractiveWorkflow):

    @workflows.workflow.entrypoint
    async def run(self) -> workflows_mistralai.ChatAssistantWorkflowOutput:
        expense = await self.wait_for_input(
            ExpenseForm,
            label="Submit Expense",
        )

        if not validate_expense(expense):
            return workflows_mistralai.ChatAssistantWorkflowOutput(
                content=[
                    workflows_mistralai.TextOutput(
                        text="Expense validation failed."
                    )
                ],
                isError=True,
            )

        return workflows_mistralai.ChatAssistantWorkflowOutput(
            content=[
                workflows_mistralai.TextOutput(
                    text=f"Expense {expense.receipt_id} is valid."
                )
            ]
        )
```

Key points:

- `FormInput` defines the structured form; `wait_for_input(...)` renders it in Vibe Work.
- `TextField(pattern=...)` applies regex validation. The example accepts IDs such as `RCP-123456`.
- `isError=True` marks the workflow as failed. The `TextOutput` text becomes the failure message shown in the conversation.

Documentation: [Forms and confirmations](https://docs.mistral.ai/studio/workflows/interacting-with-workflows/conversational_workflows/forms_and_confirmations) and [Publish in Vibe — Error handling](https://docs.mistral.ai/studio/workflows/interacting-with-workflows/conversational_workflows/publish_in_vibe).
